IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. FILEIO.
AUTHOR. SOMEONE.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
CONFIGURATION SECTION.
SPECIAL-NAMES.
    DECIMAL-POINT IS COMMA.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO "input.dat"
        ORGANIZATION IS LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS IN-STATUS.
    SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "output.dat"
        ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL.
    SELECT IDX-FILE ASSIGN TO "idx.dat"
        ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
        ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
        RECORD KEY IS IDX-KEY.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD IN-FILE.
01 IN-REC     PIC X(80).
FD OUT-FILE
    RECORD CONTAINS 40 CHARACTERS.
01 OUT-REC.
   05 OUT-ID     PIC 9(5).
   05 OUT-NAME   PIC X(35).
FD IDX-FILE.
01 IDX-REC.
   05 IDX-KEY    PIC X(8).
   05 IDX-DATA   PIC X(32).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 IN-STATUS  PIC XX.
01 EOF-FLAG   PIC X VALUE "N".
   88 AT-EOF  VALUE "Y".
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE
    OPEN I-O IDX-FILE
    PERFORM UNTIL AT-EOF
        READ IN-FILE INTO OUT-REC
            AT END SET AT-EOF TO TRUE
            NOT AT END
                WRITE OUT-REC
                MOVE OUT-ID TO IDX-KEY
                WRITE IDX-REC INVALID KEY DISPLAY "dup" END-WRITE
        END-READ
    END-PERFORM
    MOVE "KEY00001" TO IDX-KEY
    READ IDX-FILE KEY IS IDX-KEY
        INVALID KEY DISPLAY "none"
    END-READ
    REWRITE IDX-REC
    DELETE IDX-FILE RECORD
    CLOSE IN-FILE OUT-FILE IDX-FILE
    STOP RUN.
